\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  God's love is fully felt in my heart;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 far back as from the olden days.
\par That I shall look for eternal things
\par when I am in this state of flesh.
\par It struggles to have it on hand
\par :/: and that it cannot be so free :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Behold, I am someone who knows God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 But I have missed and lost the way,
\par There's nothing that can comfort my soul
\par and make my spirit feel so free.
\par In you alone I feel so free
\par :/: and so draw me so close to you :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  My father, draw me close to your Son
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj that if not, then I can get lost.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Let Him give to me a strong faith
\par    that I will stay in Him alone.
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 Through that I wish to be for Him
\par :/: and He shall also be for me :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  How can these earthly things that I see
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0\qj Be useful to me in my death
\par If these things are full in my mansions,
\par What profit can I gain from them?
\par The heart that may believe in Him
\par :/: shall be so worthy too for me :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  And so in you I shall always dwell
\par \pard\li360\sl190\slmult0 because your power is so great
\par O, Jesus, even in my death
\par You gave me all support I need
\par your words console me in my soul:
\par :/: come enter into your Kingdom :/:
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

